# FPGA-Image-Enhancement

## Quantization-Aware Residual CNN for FPGA-Based Image Enhancement

FPGA-accelerated image enhancement pipeline using residual CNN architectures, INT8 quantization, and Vitis AI deployment workflow optimized for hardware-efficient inference execution.

The project focuses on preserving enhancement residual quality during low-precision INT8 deployment so that restoration performance remains stable under FPGA inference constraints.

---

# Overview

This repository contains deployment-oriented implementations and inference workflows for FPGA-based image enhancement using quantized residual CNN architectures.

The system is designed to restore degraded images affected by noise, blur, low-light degradation, and complex real-world artifacts while maintaining efficient inference performance on FPGA hardware platforms.

The workflow includes:

* Residual CNN-based image enhancement
* Quantization-aware optimization
* INT8 deployment using Vitis AI
* FPGA-compatible `.xmodel` generation
* DPU-oriented inference execution
* PSNR / SSIM evaluation workflows
* Hardware acceleration benchmarking

The repository includes:

* trained PyTorch models (`.pth`)
* FPGA deployment models (`.xmodel`)
* inference scripts
* deployment workflows
* Docker execution environment
* runtime validation outputs
* evaluation artifacts
* FPGA deployment documentation
* project report and benchmarking analysis

---

# Key Features

* FPGA-oriented AI deployment workflow
